# Cursor safety non-parity note (blueprint safety compile)

Cursor has no permission, deny-rule, or sandbox surface blueprint can
compile .blueprint/safety.toml [deny].write into. On Cursor these deny
globs are documented intent only — nothing on this host enforces them:

- `.env*`
- `**/secrets/**`
- `.github/workflows/**`

Backstop: the verify-side tamper layer (`blueprint verify`) hashes the
protected files and fails the change on any drift, on every host.
